    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d102">

                <pb facs="0132" n="82" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg82"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.51/378</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Francis</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-10-26T14:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 26,
                                1918, 2 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>324. Answering your 513, October 24, 3 p.m. Following is summary of memorandum
                    delivered to British Embassy, October 21, in regard to a proposal on the part of
                    the British Government to establish in the Archangel and Murmansk districts of
                    Russia a new currency redeemable at a fixed rate in pounds sterling.</p>
                <p>[Here follows summary of memorandum of October 21 to the British Embassy, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg77">page 77</ref>.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
